            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted on 19/03/2025 with an acute exacerbation of his known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and routine blood tests, confirming an infective exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or acute heart failure. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a course of systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone), and supplemental oxygen therapy. He responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function. He was discharged on 20/03/2025 in stable condition. Please ensure continuation of his inhaler regimen and arrange early follow-up. Discharge medications and further recommendations are enclosed.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
